[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openeverest/openeverest/issues/2851","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openeverest/openeverest","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openeverest/openeverest/issues/2851/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openeverest/openeverest/issues/2851/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openeverest/openeverest/issues/2851/events","html_url":"https://github.com/openeverest/openeverest/pull/2851","id":5108889081,"node_id":"PR_kwDOLA3Si8788JlJ","number":2851,"title":"fix(session): avoid nil pointer panic when the JWT private key PEM is invalid","user":{"login":"Atishyy27","id":142108881,"node_id":"U_kgDOCHho0Q","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/142108881?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Atishyy27","html_url":"https://github.com/Atishyy27","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Atishyy27/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Atishyy27/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Atishyy27/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Atishyy27/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Atishyy27/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Atishyy27/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Atishyy27/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Atishyy27/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Atishyy27/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-08-10T09:58:20Z","updated_at":"2026-08-10T13:30:51Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openeverest/openeverest/pulls/2851","html_url":"https://github.com/openeverest/openeverest/pull/2851","diff_url":"https://github.com/openeverest/openeverest/pull/2851.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/openeverest/openeverest/pull/2851.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"## What\r\n\r\n`getPrivateKey()` in `pkg/session/manager.go` decoded the everest JWT signing key with `pem.Decode()` and dereferenced the result without checking for `nil`. `pem.Decode` returns a `nil` block (with a `nil` error) when it can't find a valid PEM block, so an empty, truncated, or otherwise invalid key file crashed the whole server with a nil pointer panic instead of a clean startup error.\r\n\r\nThis PR:\r\n- extracts the decode+parse step into a small `parsePrivateKeyPEM()` helper\r\n- checks for a `nil` block after `pem.Decode` and returns a descriptive error instead of panicking\r\n- wraps the `x509.ParsePKCS1PrivateKey` error instead of returning it bare, so a malformed-but-present PEM block also gets a clear message\r\n- adds `TestParsePrivateKeyPEM` covering a valid key, empty input, non-PEM input, and a PEM block that isn't a valid PKCS1 key\r\n\r\n## Why\r\n\r\n`getPrivateKey()` runs inside `session.New()`, i.e. on every everest-server startup. Any deployment issue that leaves `/etc/jwt/id_rsa` empty or corrupted (bad secret, manual edit, partial write) currently takes the whole process down with an unhelpful panic instead of a clear \"invalid JWT private key\" error.\r\n\r\n## Testing\r\n\r\n- `go build ./...`\r\n- `go test ./pkg/session/...`: new test panics on the old code (nil pointer dereference at the old `block.Bytes` line) and passes cleanly after the fix; full package suite passes\r\n\r\nFixes #2850\r\n","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openeverest/openeverest/issues/2851/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openeverest/openeverest/issues/2851/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openeverest/openeverest/issues/2850","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openeverest/openeverest","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openeverest/openeverest/issues/2850/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openeverest/openeverest/issues/2850/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openeverest/openeverest/issues/2850/events","html_url":"https://github.com/openeverest/openeverest/issues/2850","id":5108830731,"node_id":"I_kwDOLA3Si88AAAABMIKSCw","number":2850,"title":"session: getPrivateKey panics with a nil pointer dereference on an invalid JWT private key file","user":{"login":"Atishyy27","id":142108881,"node_id":"U_kgDOCHho0Q","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/142108881?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Atishyy27","html_url":"https://github.com/Atishyy27","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Atishyy27/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Atishyy27/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Atishyy27/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Atishyy27/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Atishyy27/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Atishyy27/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Atishyy27/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Atishyy27/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Atishyy27/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":6392996828,"node_id":"LA_kwDOLA3Si88AAAABfQ1j3A","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openeverest/openeverest/labels/bug","name":"bug","color":"d73a4a","default":true,"description":"Something isn't working"},{"id":6646254194,"node_id":"LA_kwDOLA3Si88AAAABjCXKcg","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openeverest/openeverest/labels/go","name":"go","color":"16e2e2","default":false,"description":"Pull requests that update Go code"},{"id":11598729211,"node_id":"LA_kwDOLA3Si88AAAACs1aP-w","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openeverest/openeverest/labels/v1","name":"v1","color":"223d9d","default":false,"description":"Only related to version 1"},{"id":11598729858,"node_id":"LA_kwDOLA3Si88AAAACs1aSgg","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openeverest/openeverest/labels/v2","name":"v2","color":"a0c21d","default":false,"description":"Only related to version 2"},{"id":11716155422,"node_id":"LA_kwDOLA3Si88AAAACulZYHg","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openeverest/openeverest/labels/triage/accepted","name":"triage/accepted","color":"0e8a16","default":false,"description":"Reviewed and accepted; this should be done"}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":1,"created_at":"2026-08-10T09:50:51Z","updated_at":"2026-08-10T10:36:55Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"﻿### What is the issue?\n\nin `pkg/session/manager.go`, `getPrivateKey()` reads the everest JWT signing key from disk and decodes it like this:\n\n```go\nfunc getPrivateKey() (*rsa.PrivateKey, error) {\n\tpemString, err := os.ReadFile(common.EverestJWTPrivateKeyFile)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn nil, errors.Join(err, errors.New(\"failed to read JWT private key\"))\n\t}\n\tblock, _ := pem.Decode(pemString)\n\treturn x509.ParsePKCS1PrivateKey(block.Bytes)\n}\n```\n\n`pem.Decode` returns a nil block (with a nil error) whenever it can't find a valid PEM block in the input. the code never checks for that and goes straight to `block.Bytes`, so any time `common.EverestJWTPrivateKeyFile` (`/etc/jwt/id_rsa`) exists but doesn't contain a valid PEM block, this panics with a nil pointer dereference instead of returning an error.\n\n`getPrivateKey()` runs inside `session.New()`, which is called once per everest-server startup, so this takes down the whole process. an empty file, a truncated write, or a manually edited `everest-jwt` secret would all crash the server with an unhelpful panic instead of a clear \"invalid JWT private key\" error.\n\n### Steps to Reproduce\n\nfound this reading the code, not from a running cluster. reproduced with a go unit test that calls the pem-decode-and-parse step directly with non-PEM input:\n\n1. checkout main\n2. call the equivalent of `parsePrivateKeyPEM([]byte(\"this is not a PEM encoded private key\"))` (i.e. `pem.Decode` + `x509.ParsePKCS1PrivateKey(block.Bytes)` with no nil check on `block`)\n3. run it\n\nthe same thing happens for real whenever `/etc/jwt/id_rsa` doesn't hold a valid PEM block, e.g. an empty secret, a partially-written file, or a bad manual edit of the `everest-jwt` secret.\n\n### Relevant Logs / Output\n\n```\npanic: runtime error: invalid memory address or nil pointer dereference\n[signal 0xc0000005 code=0x0 addr=0x18 pc=0x7ff78e2a0178]\n\ngoroutine 90 [running]:\npanic({0x7ff78e540f80?, 0x7ff78fe81f90?})\n\tC:/Program Files/Go/src/runtime/panic.go:860 +0x13a\ngithub.com/percona/everest/pkg/session.parsePrivateKeyPEM(...)\n\tpkg/session/manager.go:185 +0x18\nFAIL\tgithub.com/percona/everest/pkg/session\t33.274s\n```\n(captured locally with `go test ./pkg/session/...` against a small helper I extracted from `getPrivateKey()` to isolate the decode step; same call path as the unmodified function on main)\n\n### OpenEverest Version\n\nmain branch (tested against commit d0fb75c)\n\n### Installation Method\n\nCompiled from source (found via code review + a local `go test` run, not a running deployment)\n\n### Kubernetes Distribution\n\nOther (please specify below)\n\n### Environment Details\n\nnot cluster- or OS-dependent. this is a pure Go bug in JWT key parsing, triggered whenever the file at `common.EverestJWTPrivateKeyFile` (`/etc/jwt/id_rsa`) does not contain a valid PEM-encoded block.\n\n### Possible Solution\n\ncheck `block == nil` right after `pem.Decode` and return a descriptive error instead of falling through to `block.Bytes`. also worth wrapping the `x509.ParsePKCS1PrivateKey` error instead of returning it bare, so a malformed-but-present PEM block gets a clear message too.\n\nhappy to open a small PR for this with a regression test.\n\n### Additional Context\n\nthis only affects the failure path (missing/empty/corrupted key file). deployments with a normally-generated key are unaffected.\n\r\n","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openeverest/openeverest/issues/2850/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openeverest/openeverest/issues/2850/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openeverest/openeverest/issues/2848","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openeverest/openeverest","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openeverest/openeverest/issues/2848/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openeverest/openeverest/issues/2848/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openeverest/openeverest/issues/2848/events","html_url":"https://github.com/openeverest/openeverest/pull/2848","id":5107762949,"node_id":"PR_kwDOLA3Si8784kU7","number":2848,"title":"Pitr","user":{"login":"solovevayaroslavna","id":90199600,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwMTk5NjAw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/90199600?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/solovevayaroslavna","html_url":"https://github.com/solovevayaroslavna","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/solovevayaroslavna/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/solovevayaroslavna/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/solovevayaroslavna/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/solovevayaroslavna/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/solovevayaroslavna/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/solovevayaroslavna/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/solovevayaroslavna/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/solovevayaroslavna/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/solovevayaroslavna/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":10082777003,"node_id":"LA_kwDOLA3Si88AAAACWPr3qw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openeverest/openeverest/labels/ui","name":"ui","color":"1fa80a","default":false,"description":"Requests related to the UI"}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-08-10T07:36:13Z","updated_at":"2026-08-10T11:16:33Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openeverest/openeverest/pulls/2848","html_url":"https://github.com/openeverest/openeverest/pull/2848","diff_url":"https://github.com/openeverest/openeverest/pull/2848.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/openeverest/openeverest/pull/2848.patch","merged_at":null},"body":null,"closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openeverest/openeverest/issues/2848/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openeverest/openeverest/issues/2848/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openeverest/openeverest/issues/2847","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openeverest/openeverest","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openeve