:"https://github.com/openeverest/openeverest/pull/2841.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"Fixes #2839\n\nWhen GitHub rejects an assignment, the workflow keeps the existing fallback message for self-assignment. For maintainer delegation (`/assign @someone`), it addresses the requested assignee and explains that they may need to comment on the issue first or be a repository collaborator.\n\nValidation:\n- Ran the workflow's embedded `github-script` against mocked rejected self-assignment and delegated-assignment scenarios.\n\nAI assistance: Codex helped inspect the workflow and prepare the small regression harness. I reviewed the change and test result.","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openeverest/openeverest/issues/2841/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openeverest/openeverest/issues/2841/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openeverest/openeverest/issues/2839","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openeverest/openeverest","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openeverest/openeverest/issues/2839/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openeverest/openeverest/issues/2839/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openeverest/openeverest/issues/2839/events","html_url":"https://github.com/openeverest/openeverest/issues/2839","id":5103272341,"node_id":"I_kwDOLA3Si88AAAABMC3BlQ","number":2839,"title":"assign bot reports the wrong reason and the wrong person when a maintainer assigns someone else","user":{"login":"recharte","id":16167419,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MTY3NDE5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16167419?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/recharte","html_url":"https://github.com/recharte","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/recharte/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/recharte/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/recharte/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/recharte/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/recharte/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/recharte/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/recharte/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/recharte/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/recharte/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":6392996828,"node_id":"LA_kwDOLA3Si88AAAABfQ1j3A","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openeverest/openeverest/labels/bug","name":"bug","color":"d73a4a","default":true,"description":"Something isn't working"},{"id":6392996838,"node_id":"LA_kwDOLA3Si88AAAABfQ1j5g","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openeverest/openeverest/labels/good%20first%20issue","name":"good first issue","color":"7057ff","default":true,"description":"Good for newcomers"},{"id":6646251284,"node_id":"LA_kwDOLA3Si88AAAABjCW_FA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openeverest/openeverest/labels/github_actions","name":"github_actions","color":"000000","default":false,"description":"Pull requests that update GitHub Actions code"},{"id":11716155422,"node_id":"LA_kwDOLA3Si88AAAACulZYHg","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openeverest/openeverest/labels/triage/accepted","name":"triage/accepted","color":"0e8a16","default":false,"description":"Reviewed and accepted; this should be done"}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[{"login":"julismo","id":64311197,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0MzExMTk3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64311197?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/julismo","html_url":"https://github.com/julismo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/julismo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/julismo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/julismo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/julismo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/julismo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/julismo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/julismo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/julismo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/julismo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}],"milestone":null,"comments":2,"created_at":"2026-08-09T15:24:12Z","updated_at":"2026-08-09T15:33:57Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":{"login":"julismo","id":64311197,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0MzExMTk3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64311197?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/julismo","html_url":"https://github.com/julismo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/julismo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/julismo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/julismo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/julismo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/julismo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/julismo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/julismo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/julismo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/julismo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### What is the issue?\n\n`assign.yml` verifies the assignment took effect and replies on failure, but the failure message is written for the self-assign path only:\n\n```js\nawait reply(`@${commenter} I couldn't assign this to you — GitHub rejected the assignment. A maintainer will pick this up shortly.`);\n```\n\nWhen a maintainer uses the `@handle` form, all three parts are wrong: it addresses the commenter rather than the target, says \"to you\" about a third party, and tells a maintainer that a maintainer will pick it up.\n\nIt also omits the only actionable part — *why* GitHub rejected it. In practice the cause is almost always that the target is not a collaborator and hasn't commented on that issue, since GitHub only accepts assignees who have participated in the thread. That's fixable in seconds if you know it, and opaque if you don't.\n\nSeen on #2236, where the target had commented on the linked PR but never on the issue itself.\n\n### Possible Solution\n\nBranch the message on whether `target === commenter`, and name the likely cause in the delegated case — something along the lines of: the target needs to comment on the issue first, because GitHub only accepts assignees who are collaborators or thread participants.","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openeverest/openeverest/issues/2839/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openeverest/openeverest/issues/2839/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openeverest/openeverest/issues/2837","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openeverest/openeverest","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openeverest/openeverest/issues/2837/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openeverest/openeverest/issues/2837/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openeverest/openeverest/issues/2837/events","html_url":"https://github.com/openeverest/openeverest/pull/2837","id":510321148